# Sprint 17 — Network Segmentation and Firewall Validation

## Objective

The objective of Sprint 17 was to transition the SOC home lab from a primarily flat VMware NAT network into a segmented architecture protected by a pfSense firewall.

The sprint focused on:

- Migrating corporate systems to a dedicated CORP-LAN
- Isolating the Kali Linux attack workstation on a separate ATTACK_NET
- Routing traffic between networks through pfSense
- Restoring Active Directory connectivity after the network migration
- Updating Splunk forwarding for the new addressing scheme
- Implementing least-privilege firewall rules
- Validating permitted and denied traffic
- Troubleshooting traffic at multiple layers using firewall logs, packet captures, and rule counters

