# Implementation

## 1. pfSense Network Segmentation

FW01 was configured with three network interfaces:

```text
WAN         -> VMware NAT
LAN         -> 10.10.10.1/24
ATTACK_NET  -> 10.10.20.1/24
```

This placed pfSense between the corporate systems and the isolated testing network.

The resulting trust boundaries are:

```text
ATTACK_NET
     |
     |
     v
   FW01
     |
     |
     v
CORP-LAN
```

Traffic crossing these boundaries is subject to firewall policy.

---

## 2. CORP-LAN Migration

Corporate systems were migrated from the original VMware NAT network to:

```text
10.10.10.0/24
```

Systems were assigned the following addresses:

```text
DC01       10.10.10.10
SIEM01     10.10.10.20
WIN11-01   10.10.10.101
WIN11-02   10.10.10.102
```

The pfSense LAN interface became the default gateway:

```text
10.10.10.1
```

Domain-connected Windows systems use DC01 for DNS:

```text
10.10.10.10
```

---

## 3. Active Directory Validation

After migration, domain connectivity was tested from the Windows endpoints.

One workstation initially reported a broken secure channel.

Testing included:

```powershell
Test-ComputerSecureChannel -Verbose
```

The workstation's connectivity to DC01 and domain services was restored and the secure channel was validated.

An important operational observation was that domain-dependent tests require DC01 to be running. A failed secure-channel test while the domain controller is offline does not necessarily indicate that the workstation trust relationship itself is damaged.

---

## 4. Splunk Migration

SIEM01 was migrated to:

```text
10.10.10.20
```

Splunk Universal Forwarder configurations on Windows endpoints were updated to use the new Splunk receiver address.

Example:

```ini
[tcpout]
defaultGroup = default-autolb-group

[tcpout:default-autolb-group]
server = 10.10.10.20:9997

[tcpout-server://10.10.10.20:9997]
```

Connectivity was validated against:

```text
TCP/9997
```

The Splunk receiver was confirmed listening on the expected port.

Firewall configuration was also validated when endpoint-to-SIEM connectivity initially failed.

