# Security Principles Demonstrated

## Network Segmentation

Corporate and security-testing systems operate on separate Layer 3 networks.

## Least Privilege

ATTACK_NET was not given unrestricted access to CORP-LAN.

Only specifically required traffic was permitted.

## Defense in Depth

Traffic must satisfy both:

1. pfSense network firewall policy
2. Windows endpoint firewall policy

## Default Deny

Traffic not explicitly permitted from ATTACK_NET remains blocked.

## Logging and Visibility

Firewall logging and rule counters provide evidence of traffic matching security policy.

## Packet-Level Troubleshooting

Packet capture was used to identify exactly where communication stopped rather than relying solely on application-level connectivity tests.

